module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.build_cache_key_includes_the_absolute_checkout_path

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data build_cache_key_includes_the_absolute_checkout_path: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "build_cache_key_includes_the_absolute_checkout_path" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a content cache whose key includes an input the identity does not mean never serves the second identity: two compute identities build the SAME commit, but each checks out at its own absolute path (gunbc.compute.work_provider_local ComputeLayout checkout = <root>/compute/work/<identity>/src), and sccache's Rust compilation key carries the absolute source and working-directory paths. The two builds are one computation (std.computation_identity) answered as two cache keys, so every rustc invocation of the second identity misses. Nothing refuses and nothing is wrong in the output: the cost is paid silently, as a full cold Rust build per identity.",

    "SPECIMEN AND CAUSE CONFIRMATION, found 2026-10-16. //gunbc/instruments:compute-run-unit-cold (#14149, run 38858207563) built two identities back to back in one dispatch on one sccache server read through the unit's own ExecStop=: the second identity had hits=25 (Assembler 12, C/C++ 13) and Rust 0/111. The cause was INFERRED, not observed. //gunbc/instruments:compute-run-unit-cold-same-path (run 38863461852) built ONE identity twice at the SAME absolute checkout, removing the checkout and moving the target aside between builds so the second cargo run was cold: build 1 Rust hits 0, misses 111; build 2 Rust hits 111, misses 0 (Cache hits (Rust) 111, rate 100.00%), with Assembler 12 and C/C++ 13 unchanged. That control holds identity equal to path, so it could not separate them. The four-arm run 38867404661 (head 3cc1d2506a) did: A1 0/111, A2 (same identity, same path, same root) 111/111, B (DIFFERENT identity at the SAME checkout path) 0/111, C (same identity at a different path) 0/111. So the checkout path alone is NOT sufficient. Run 38874802505 (head cbcdb90315) added two controls run sequentially with A's target directory forced: D (different identity B at PA, A's target) 111/0 and E (identity A at a different path PC, A's target) 104 hits / 7 misses. So the cargo target directory enters the key for all 111 Rust compilations (D reuses everything with identity and path of A's build both absent from the difference; B and C, which changed the target, got 0), and the checkout path enters it for the remaining 7 (E loses exactly those). Both prefixes must be stripped or held constant for the second identity to reuse the first. THE KEY INPUTS ARE NOW OBSERVED. sccache 0.15.0 hashes every CARGO_-prefixed environment variable (src/compiler/rust.rs generate_hash_key; extdeps.cache.sccache sccache_rust_key_facts), so the unit's CARGO_TARGET_DIR was the input for 104 crates; cargo's own CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR carries the checkout for the workspace crates. Moving the target to cargo --target-dir (the one target authority; run 38882112700, head 4ee0cd774a) took B and C from 0/111 to 95/111, leaving 16 misses named from the unit's own server log: the 7 path-sensitive crates (proc_macro2 and the workspace crates v1_compiler, v1_stage0_extdeps_languages, v1_stage0_runtime, v1_stage0_std_core, v1_stage0_std_surface, v1_stage0_v1_artifact, v1_stage0_v1_infer; CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR under the checkout) and 9 registry crates (im, serde, serde_core, serde_json, serde_spanned, toml, toml_datetime, toml_edit, ureq) whose build scripts put OUT_DIR under the per-identity target; a local toy reproduces the mechanism (a build-script crate hits across target dirs unless it reads env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), when it misses). Remaining fix: present stable in-unit paths for checkout and target (per-unit private BindPaths), not yet probed.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the non-Rust hits (Assembler, C/C++) survive distinct paths because those keys are path-independent, so a nonzero overall hit rate reads as reuse working while the Rust share, the dominant cost, is 0. A total hit count therefore cannot be the observation; the per-language line (Cache hits (Rust)) is. Neighbour, not this class: a shared writable target directory (C4, #14040), which is cross-identity reuse that is UNSAFE; this class is cross-identity reuse that is MISSING.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The failure occurs on every second identity and is contained only by the cost being paid, not refused. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The path is a declared input of the layout, so a checkout path (or a path-prefix remapping) that is a function of the commit and not of the identity can be derived from the model, and an expected-red requiring Rust hits > 0 on the second identity discriminates it. It is not structurally impossible while rustc's key admits any absolute path. NEXT TRIGGER (can climb after C4, #14040, lands, which fixes the per-identity target layout the fix must sit on): a layout in which two identities of one commit present the same source path to rustc, whether by a stable checkout path or --remap-path-prefix, whichever extdeps.cache, extdeps.rust/cargo and gunbc.owned_cargo_target already declare, without reintroducing a shared writable target and without breaking //gunbc/instruments:compute-wrong-capture.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
